menu "Shelly diagnostics"

    config SHELLY_DIAG_LOG
        bool "Diagnostics log on the Wi-Fi mode page"
        default n
        help
            Keep the last 6 KB of the log in memory that survives a restart,
            and show it on the Wi-Fi maintenance page (Diagnostics log). It
            also logs heap and Thread/IP state every few seconds while pairing,
            and freezes the log 5 s after a failed pairing. Costs 6 KB of heap
            for the whole run. For troubleshooting builds only: see docs/BUILDING.md.

endmenu

menu "Shelly device type"

    config SHELLY_HAS_OPENER_MODE
        bool "Offer a garage door opener mode on the Wi-Fi mode page"
        default n
        help
            For a one-relay board with a dry contact: the Wi-Fi mode page lets
            the owner choose what the relay is for, an outlet (on or off) or a
            garage door opener (a short pulse per toggle). Both use the same
            Matter endpoints, so changing it keeps the pairing. The choice is
            saved with 3 presses of the button and kept through factory
            resets. A build without Wi-Fi mode is always an outlet.

    config SHELLY_PULSE_MS
        int "Opener pulse length (ms)"
        depends on SHELLY_HAS_OPENER_MODE
        default 500
        range 100 5000
        help
            How long the relay stays closed for one trigger in opener mode.

endmenu
